From 436792ce37cf3ff041757fdba7f40b1996a5ca01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dinakaran <dinakaranvijayakumar@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:02:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] loams-pg18: the read stream keeps the smgr it is given

The port of 65c4e46baf (no readahead assumption for temporary
relations) carried 17's "smgr = RelationGetSmgr(rel);" into 18's
read_stream_begin_impl(), which takes the smgr as an argument and has
no relation for smgr-only streams (read_stream_begin_smgr_relation, as
CREATE DATABASE's RelationCopyStorageUsingBuffer uses): a NULL
dereference. The line goes; the temporary-relation check uses the
persistence argument.

Loams-Patch: LP-0038
Signed-off-by: Dinakaran <dinakaranvijayakumar@outlook.com>
---
 src/backend/storage/aio/read_stream.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/storage/aio/read_stream.c b/src/backend/storage/aio/read_stream.c
index 3daaad6..043c2b2 100644
--- a/src/backend/storage/aio/read_stream.c
+++ b/src/backend/storage/aio/read_stream.c
@@ -568,8 +568,6 @@ read_stream_begin_impl(int flags,
 	uint32		max_possible_buffer_limit;
 	Oid			tablespace_id;
 
-	smgr = RelationGetSmgr(rel);
-
 	/*
 	 * Reject attempts to read non-local temporary relations; we would be
 	 * likely to get wrong data since we have no visibility into the owning
-- 
2.55.0

